@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}
<div class="mid stack">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">About this project</p>
        <h1>Online Banking</h1>
        <p class="muted">A demo internet-banking site built with ASP.NET Core MVC. The server renders every page with Razor views, so there's no separate frontend app.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>What you can do</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Customers</strong> sign up, apply for a savings or current account (with KYC details), see balances, filter and download statements, and transfer money with a transaction PIN.</li>
            <li><strong>Bank staff</strong> review applications, open accounts with an opening deposit, post cash deposits and withdrawals, freeze or close accounts, and read customer messages.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h2>How it's built</h2>
        <dl class="dl">
            <dt>Web</dt><dd>ASP.NET Core MVC (.NET 10), Razor views, Areas for the admin console</dd>
            <dt>Data</dt><dd>Entity Framework Core with SQLite; money stored as whole paise; optimistic concurrency on balances</dd>
            <dt>Security</dt><dd>Cookie authentication with roles, hashed passwords and PINs, antiforgery tokens on every form, security headers</dd>
            <dt>Rules</dt><dd>Insufficient-funds checks, ₹2,00,000 daily transfer limit, PIN lockout, frozen accounts, idempotent transfers</dd>
            <dt>Quality</dt><dd>xUnit tests for the banking rules, end-to-end browser test, GitHub Actions, Docker</dd>
        </dl>
    </div>

    <p class="muted small">This started in 2022 as an ASP.NET MVC 5 (.NET Framework) project and was rebuilt in 2026 on ASP.NET Core so it can run on Linux and be hosted for free.</p>
</div>
